Nuclear imaging equipment encompasses a family of sophisticated diagnostic devices that employ radioactive tracers to visualize physiological and metabolic processes within the human body. The portfolio includes Positron Emission Tomography (PET) scanners, Single Photon Emission Computed Tomography (SPECT) systems, hybrid modalities such as PET/CT and SPECT/CT, as well as cyclotrons and radiopharmaceutical generators crucial for tracer production. By delivering functional insights that complement anatomical imaging, these technologies enable clinicians to detect cancer, cardiovascular disorders, and neurological conditions with unparalleled precision, guide treatment planning, and monitor therapeutic outcomes.
