What is Nuclear Imaging Equipment?
Nuclear imaging equipment represents a convergence of radiopharmaceutical science and advanced detector engineering. PET scanners capture annihilation photons emitted by positron-emitting isotopes, delivering high‑resolution metabolic maps. SPECT systems detect gamma photons from single‑photon emitters, providing functional information with a broader range of tracers. Hybrid platforms such as PET/CT and SPECT/CT fuse functional data with CT‑derived anatomical detail, while emerging PET/MRI solutions combine metabolic insight with superior soft‑tissue contrast. In addition, cyclotrons and generator units ensure on‑site production of short‑lived isotopes, supporting a continuous supply chain essential for clinical workflow.
