Key Market Drivers
1. Rising Clinical Demand for Advanced Diagnostics
The global increase in cancer incidence, cardiovascular disease burden, and neurodegenerative disorders is compelling hospitals to adopt high‑precision imaging modalities. Early detection and quantitative assessment of disease activity are now standard expectations, encouraging procurement of state‑of‑the‑art PET and SPECT systems.
2. Technological Innovation and Cost Efficiency
Solid‑state detector breakthroughs, time‑of‑flight (TOF) capabilities, and AI‑driven image reconstruction are shortening acquisition times and lowering radiation doses. These efficiencies improve patient throughput and reduce per‑study costs, making advanced nuclear imaging attractive even to budget‑conscious providers.
